{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgS1sUQr2krR4UULGbngr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The second publish returned 500 because `similarity()` in `src/app.py` produces a float, and boto3 refuses to write floats to DynamoDB. The three tests pass, including two new ones for the second-publish case. I couldn't run a publish against a real table here.\n\n**Cause:** `similarity()` returned `round(..., 4)`, a float, and `publish()` stores that score inside `similar` via `put_item`. On the first publish the table is empty, so `similar` is `[]` and no float is written. From the second publish on there are matches, so `put_item` raises `TypeError: Float types are not supported`, which matches `logs/error.log`.\n\n**Fix:** `similarity()` now returns an integer percent (`round(100 * ...)`), which DynamoDB accepts. Any consumer of `score` now sees whole percents from 0 to 100 instead of a 0–1 fraction.\n\n**Why it can't come back:** the new tests publish a second story into a populated table and check the score is an `int`. They also check the handler returns 201 twice. The test table rejects floats the way boto3 does, so putting a float back fails the tests.\n\n**Colleague's note:** I used the diagnosis, the integer-percent fix, and the advice to seed the table before testing a write. I skipped the codebase grep (I just read `src/app.py`, which is the whole service) and the real-table publish. `ANSWER.md` says which parts applied.\n\n**Not changed:** `publish()` does one `scan` without pagination, so once the table passes 1 MB the related-story list will be computed from partial data. I noted this in `ANSWER.md` as a separate issue.\n\nI haven't committed anything."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1147,"cache_read_input_tokens":25726,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1147},"output_tokens":544,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7fb84099-5ba1-445a-a47d-fa90209c433a","uuid":"1ce0b940-33de-4755-b5ce-572ec4c3bf6b","timestamp":"2026-10-27T03:16:13.696Z","request_id":"req_011CgS1sU8yUTpS2d85VAeMV"}
